ohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["_help_route._REMOVED_SPELLINGS includes both `\"compact\": \"rebar store compact <id>\"` and `\"compact-all\": \"rebar store compact --all\"` (src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py:61-62)","docs/exit-codes.md:121: '`compact` → `store compact <id>`; `compact-all` → `store compact --all`'","The plan's grep alternation contains `compact-all` but not a bare `compact`; the per-verb negative lookahead `(?![a-zA-Z0-9_-])` prevents the `compact-all` token from ever matching a bare `rebar compact` reference","Plan states the 20 pairs are 'story 1's 11 and story 2's 9' — the 9 explicitly includes `compact`"],"finding":"The Testing-section residual grep omits the bare `compact` spelling from its verb alternation (it lists `compact-all` only), so the mechanism that is supposed to confirm 'the code stories left nothing to teach' cannot catch a stray `rebar compact <id>` reference. `compact` is one of story 2's nine storage-maintenance removed spellings in `_help_route._REMOVED_SPELLINGS` and is documented as removed in docs/exit-codes.md:121.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f664b74b1fb726a2c","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing section (residual git grep) and AC 'The residual grep above prints nothing'","norm_id":"nc0cd218ffbfa48d2","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A teaching surface still says `rebar compact <id>` after story 2; the residual grep prints nothing and the AC passes while a stale removed-verb reference survives."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Insert `compact` into the alternation, e.g. `...|export|import|compact|compact-all)...` (order does not matter given the trailing negative lookahead).","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committe